// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/analog/accept_sar.t27 -- the per-block acceptance checks of the external team's report of 2026-10-16, as an evaluator, applied to our SAR ADC blocks
; M5c of the analog emulation epic (#10486, issue #11212, night loop #11063). The external team's report of 2026-10-16 lists, for the 13 blocks of the golden SAR ADC, a
; measured value and the limit that its check enforces (conditions: tt corner, 27 C, VDD 1.5 V, cells taken from the integrated converter's netlist). The team
; confirmed on 2026-10-20 that the checks and their limits may be used and published in this repository. This file holds those limits as named constants, one
; pure check function per quantity, and one function per block that MEASURES the quantity on OUR model, by `use` of the spec that holds the model (no copy), and
; applies the check to it. The report is cited as "the external team's report of 2026-10-16" and nowhere else; no person or company is named.
; -
; THE VERDICT RULE, and why it is strict. A row is one quantity of the report's check. Its verdict is PASS (our model produced the value and it is inside the limit),
; FAIL (our model produced the value and it is outside) or NOT MODELLED (our model does not produce the quantity the check enforces; nothing is compared, and the row is
; never a PASS, whatever a constant might have said: as_verdict(false, x) is NOT MODELLED for both x). A block is FAIL when any of its rows FAILs, PASS when it has
; rows and every row is PASS, and NOT MODELLED otherwise: a block whose threshold passes and whose delay is not modelled is not a pass. A FAIL is a measurement and is
; reported as measured; no model was tuned in this file to turn one into a PASS.
; -
; THE LEVEL OF EACH MODEL, and what it means for the verdict (the doc docs/analog/accept-sar-2026-10-20.md has the table with the numbers).
;   inverter           PSP103 tables of the SG13G2 NMOS (W 1.0 um) and PMOS (W 3.0 um), tt, 27 C, current in the log domain (M3c-2, mos_psp103.t27): its DC transfer gives the
;                      switching threshold. The delays into 20 fF are NOT MODELLED: the model's transient is validated at 500 fF and 10 pF only, and at 20 fF the gate edge
;                      kicks the output 5 times further outside the tables' range of 0 to Vdd than the 100 fF case that mos_psp103.t27 already says it cannot hold.
;   nand, nor, tgate   GATE LEVEL (sar_logic.t27): a gate is a delay and a truth table, a transmission gate a switch with a stored node. A logic value is 0, 1 or X, never a
;                      voltage. The truth table is measured and is a row of its own; the levels in volts and the tgate's Ron and leakage are NOT MODELLED.
;   dff                the same gate level (inside SAR_logic): capture, hold, set, reset and the clock-to-Q delay are measured on it; the levels in volts are NOT MODELLED.
;   dynamic_comparator PSP103 current tables at 50 C, the golden deck's temperature (sar_comparator_psp.t27), the NO-CHARGE model: the devices' own capacitance is not in it, so
;                      its decision comes 98 times too fast against ngspice (5.35 ps against 523 ps at +2 mV). The sign and the end levels are measured; the reset (a second clock
;                      phase) is not run; the decision time is measured and FAILS the 10 ps lower limit.
;   tracking_switch    SQUARE LAW (MOSFET level 1) bootstrapped switch (sar_switch.t27): the tracking error at DC is measured (1.97 uV, the arithmetic floor); the hold step and the
;                      droop are NOT MODELLED, because the square law has no gate capacitance (no charge injection) and no leakage: the model's 0.18 uV and 0 V would "pass" a
;                      30 mV and a 5 mV limit by having no effect at all, which is not a measurement of the effect.
;   clock_gen, SAR_logic  gate level with delay tables MEASURED on the golden gates in ngspice (sar_logic.t27, 113 gates); the delays are the model's own run, within 8 % of ngspice.
;   DAC_control, DAC_control_top, neg_bottom_plate_logic  NOT MODELLED. The DAC (sar_cdac.t27) has ideal capacitors driven by ideal plate sources: the level a plate reaches
;                      is its input, not an output; the latches and the N half's follow-then-complement logic are not circuits in any spec.
;   integration        the behavioural converter (sar_adc.t27): ideal DAC capacitors plus ONE fitted top-plate parasitic and the comparator offset measured on the netlist
;                      (sar_kick.t27), on an ideal sampling input. A PASS here is a PASS of that model, which was fitted to the golden deck's 30 of 31 codes; it is not a
;                      circuit-level result.
; -
; WHAT THE ROWS ARE NOT. The conditions differ in places and each is stated in the doc: the report's tracking switch drives 2 pF at 0.3 and 1.2 V, ours drives 3.93 pF at
; 0.2 and 1.3 V; the report's comparator is at 27 C, ours at 50 C (the 27 C tables give 5.12 ps and fail too); the report's ramp for the converter has 8 conversions
; whose ideal end codes are 517 and 1579, ours is the literal -1 to +1 V ramp, and the report's own ramp is rebuilt as context only. The stop time of the clock is taken
; from the eleventh Valid rise to the last clkc fall at the golden pace of 40 ns; the report's 10.7 ns is not reproduced by that definition (ours is 5.70 ns) and its
; definition is not in the material this file was made from.
; -
; THE NEGATIVE CONTROLS (FR-004), each a test that passes by seeing the failure. Every check function refuses a broken value (a delay out of range, a swapped bit, a wrong
; code) and accepts the report's own measured value, so no check is always-FAIL or always-PASS. Where a model can be broken to leave the limit, that is done too: the
; PMOS table zeroed (the output never falls through Vdd / 2: the reader returns -0.031 V, no crossing), the inputs of the comparator exchanged (the sign flips), the boost capacitor removed (tracking error 25.4 mV), the trim code
; ignored (ratio 1.0), a dff with Set and Reset exchanged (the order, the counts and the set and reset rows fail), a converter whose MSB capacitor is halved (237 LSB).
; Honest limit of the control: a few of the report's limits are wide (the inverter threshold 0.5 to 1.0 V, a bridge of 2 units gives 45.5 LSB against 64), and a model
; error inside the limit is not seen by that check; the sar_adc.t27 tests see it by the codes.
; -
; WHAT A PASS SAYS. For the clock_gen, SAR_logic and integration blocks: every quantity the report's check enforces is produced by our model and is inside the report's limit.
; For a row marked PASS inside a NOT MODELLED block: that quantity, at the model's level above, is inside the limit. WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY. Nothing about a transistor-level
; result for any gate-level block, nothing about voltage levels of any digital node, nothing about power, noise, mismatch or another corner or temperature (the report's smoke
; suite runs five corners at -40, 27 and 125 C; our tables have no -40 or 125 C and the line is NOT MODELLED), nothing about speed. The report's numbers are the report's; ours
; are computed here by the named functions. ASCII only, English only.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module AnalogAcceptSar;

